From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:46:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] downloads: hide videos from gallery apps with an unknown
 file extension
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HarmonyOS indexes the whole "兼容应用数据" tree that 卓易通 maps SAF
folders to, and its media scanner ignores .nomedia. It decides what is a
video purely by file extension, so finished downloads are now stored as
"<name>.mkv.anikku" (application/octet-stream) when the new
"Hide downloaded videos from the gallery" switch is on (default).

- Downloader.copyIntoDownloadDir appends HIDDEN_VIDEO_SUFFIX to the final
  name; resume detection and success checks already tolerate it.
- DownloadManager.buildVideo accepts both plain videos and suffixed files;
  playback goes through a content fd, so the extension is irrelevant.
- DownloadManager.applyGalleryVisibilityToDownloads renames existing files
  in both directions (uses renameToOrCopy for SAF providers that cannot
  rename); exposed in Settings > Downloads as "Rename existing downloads".
- Download cache is keyed on directory names, so nothing else changes.
